  questions:[
   {q:"In Hebrew, the Persian king Xerxes is called…", options:["Ahasuerus","Cyrus","Darius","Haman"], answer:0, boss:false, tag:"SS-CC", explain:"Ahasuerus is the Hebrew form of the name Xerxes I, who ruled Persia from 486 to 465 BC."},
   {q:"In which Persian city is most of the story of Esther set?", options:["Athens","Rome","Susa","Cairo"], answer:2, boss:false, tag:"SS-PE", explain:"Susa was one of the royal cities of Persia, used by the kings as a winter capital."},
   {q:"Who raised Esther after she was orphaned?", options:["Haman","Ezra","Daniel","Mordecai"], answer:3, boss:false, tag:"RE", explain:"Mordecai, Esther’s older cousin, brought her up and later encouraged her to speak to the king."},
   {q:"Why was it so dangerous for Esther to go to the king without being called?", options:["The king never saw anyone","Anyone who entered unsummoned could be put to death unless the king held out the sceptre","The palace was closed in winter","Only men were allowed in the hall"], answer:1, boss:false, tag:"SS-DO", teach:true, explain:"Persian court rule said that coming before the king unsummoned risked death unless he held out his golden sceptre. Esther chose to go anyway, which is what makes her so brave."},
   {q:"The villain who plotted against the Jewish people was…", options:["Nehemiah","Haman","Cyrus","Daniel"], answer:1, boss:false, tag:"RE", explain:"Haman, a powerful official, persuaded the king to sign an edict against the Jewish people, but his plot was exposed by Esther."},
   {q:"The Jewish people remember the events of Esther at the festival of…", options:["Christmas","Easter","Purim","Nowruz only"], answer:2, boss:false, tag:"RE", explain:"Purim is a Jewish festival that remembers the rescue described in the book of Esther. (Nowruz is the Persian new year, a different festival.)"},
   {q:"Lake Urmia is famous for…", options:["penguins and seals","flamingos and brine shrimp","kiwi and kākāpō","whales"], answer:1, boss:false, tag:"SC-LW-Eco", explain:"Lake Urmia is a very salty lake in north-west Iran where brine shrimp live and flamingos feed. It has shrunk a lot in recent decades."},
   {q:"BOSS ×2 — Why does a tell form?", options:["A river carries a hill to the city","People rebuild on top of old mud-brick settlements again and again","Volcanoes build mounds near cities","Kings order mounds to be built"], answer:1, boss:true, tag:"SS-PE", teach:true, explain:"Mud-brick buildings crumbled, and people levelled the ground and built on the same spot. Over centuries the layers rose into a mound called a tell, and archaeologists read the layers from top (newest) to bottom (oldest)."},
   {q:"A rhyton is…", options:["a sword","a coin","a wall","a drinking horn that ends in an animal’s head"], answer:3, boss:false, tag:"VA-UC", explain:"A rhyton is a drinking vessel that narrows to a point and ends in the head of an animal, such as a lion, ibex or griffin."},
   {q:"Review: Who named Cyrus long before he was born?", options:["Esther","Ezra","Isaiah","Haman"], answer:2, boss:false, tag:"RE", explain:"The prophet Isaiah named Cyrus as a ruler who would help God’s people, long before Cyrus was born (Isaiah 44–45)."},
   {q:"Review: Which Persian king built the Royal Road and organised the empire into provinces?", options:["Alexander","Darius I","Cyrus","Nehemiah"], answer:1, boss:false, tag:"SS-CC", explain:"Darius I organised the empire and improved the Royal Road, the highway that carried the king’s messengers (see Stage 3)."},
   {q:"BOSS ×3 — The book of Esther never names God, but the story shows…", options:["that God was absent","that the king was God","that nothing matters","God quietly working behind the scenes, through ordinary events and brave choices"], answer:3, boss:true, tag:"RE", teach:true, explain:"The ‘coincidences’ of the story, and Esther’s courage, point to providence: God quietly at work behind events. Readers explain the book’s silence about God in different ways, but many see His care in the timing."}
  ],
